{"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaxPlusSemiring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"_SemiringScalar","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SignedNumeric","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s13SignedNumericP"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"zero","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is −∞ ("},{"code":"Int.min","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"-.infinity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), "},{"code":"one","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is 0, ⊕ is "},{"code":"max","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and ⊗ is "},{"code":"+","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"code":"<","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"natural order, in which longer is better: "},{"code":"MaxPlusSemiring(9) < MaxPlusSemiring(2)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is the reverse of the values’, so "},{"code":"[a, b].max()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the shorter and "},{"code":".min()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" the longer."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"⊗ is a closed sum. −∞ (the zero) absorbs every value, and any other sum traps on integer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"overflow. A finite integer sum that lands exactly on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".min"},{"type":"text","text":" is the zero, so an edge of that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"weight carries no path. The carrier is ℝ ∪ {−∞}, without +∞. No operation checks for NaN. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ShortestPaths entry points trap on a NaN weight."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Longest paths exist where no cycle has a positive length: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dagShortestPaths"},{"type":"text","text":" gives them in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"acyclic graph, and Bellman–Ford returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" when a positive cycle is reachable. Dijkstra’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithm needs every examined weight to be at most 0."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["dag.dagShortestPaths(from: s) { MaxPlusSemiring(duration[$0]) }"],"type":"codeListing"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The max-plus semiring (max, +) over ","type":"text"},{"code":"Value","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", for longest paths, also called the arctic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"semiring.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/semirings\/maxplussemiring"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/SelectiveSemiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/SL","doc:\/\/Semirings\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/Semirings\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/Semirings\/SQ","doc:\/\/Semirings\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/Semirings\/SH","doc:\/\/Semirings\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Semirings\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"kind":"symbol","topicSection